Description: dmaengine: imx-dma: keep a cyclic transfer going past its last period
 A cyclic transfer's scatterlist is its periods and one more entry, the
 link back to the first. The table was initialised for the periods
 alone, which marks the last period as the table's end, so sg_next()
 returned NULL there and the transfer stopped after one pass of the
 buffer: on the Chumby Classic, sound played for one ALSA buffer and
 then stopped for good. The link now ends the table, and sg_chain()
 clears that mark.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
---
diff --git a/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c b/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c
index 8871750..be488a3 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c
@@ -890,7 +890,12 @@ static struct dma_async_tx_descriptor *imxdma_prep_dma_cyclic(
 	if (!imxdmac->sg_list)
 		return NULL;

-	sg_init_table(imxdmac->sg_list, periods);
+	/*
+	 * The table is the periods and the link back to the first: only the
+	 * link may end it, or sg_next() stops after the last period and the
+	 * transfer with it.
+	 */
+	sg_init_table(imxdmac->sg_list, periods + 1);

 	for (i = 0; i < periods; i++) {
 		sg_assign_page(&imxdmac->sg_list[i], NULL);
